# Azog, Moria's Ruin on Bot2's Ornithopter (power 0): X = 0, and "amass Goblins 0" still creates the 0/0 Goblin Army token when its controller has
# no Army (CR 701.47a, 701.47b: it amassed even though counters can't be put on), which is put into the graveyard by state-based actions
# (CR 704.5f) and then ceases to exist (CR 111.7). Nothing stays on Bot2's battlefield but its land; Bot1 draws nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Azog, Moria's Ruin
Plains x3
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Swamp x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Azog, Moria's Ruin.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
